<dialog id="help-dialog"><header><div><span class="eyebrow">CYBER WATCH</span><h2>Help &amp; documentation</h2></div><button type="button" data-close-help aria-label="Close help">&times;</button></header><div class="help-content"><h3>Monitor the student portal</h3><p>Log into the student portal, visit pages, or sign out. These events appear in Event Log. Five failed logins for one account and IP within ten minutes create an incident. Normal logged-out visits redirect to login without a threat incident. A signed-in student requesting the security dashboard, or an unauthenticated protected POST request, creates an access-denied incident.</p><h3>Investigate an alert</h3><p>Select an incident from the bell or the incident queue. Review its source event, IP and timeline, then save its status. Times are shown in Philippine time.</p><h3>Search records</h3><p>The top search checks event IDs, types, account identifiers and IP addresses across the last 30 days. Results are paginated in groups of 20. The Event Log's local filter only filters the current page.</p><h3>Connect Gmail notifications</h3><p>Open Gmail Alerts from the sidebar. Enter the sender Gmail address, its Google app password, and administrator recipient. Save the connection and enable automatic emails. Student recipients are read automatically from their fixed portal account emails. Review the student recipient table and delivery history; incident links open the supporting evidence.</p><p>The delivery worker runs every minute while this Windows account is logged in and MySQL is running. Failed messages retry up to three times, five minutes apart. Review delivery history for results. Anonymous incidents notify only the administrator.</p><p><a href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/185833" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google app password instructions</a></p><h3>Recipient privacy</h3><p>Send separate messages to the administrator and affected student. Student messages should describe only that student's event, without exposing other accounts or administrator evidence.</p></div></dialog>
<script>(()=>{const pairs=[['.notification-trigger','notification-panel'],['.admin-profile-trigger','admin-profile-menu']];const close=()=>pairs.forEach(([selector,id])=>{document.getElementById(id).hidden=true;document.querySelector(selector).setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');});pairs.forEach(([selector,id])=>document.querySelector(selector).addEventListener('click',()=>{const open=document.getElementById(id).hidden;close();document.getElementById(id).hidden=!open;document.querySelector(selector).setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(open));}));document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(!e.target.closest('.header-actions'))close();});document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape')close();});const dialog=document.getElementById('help-dialog');document.getElementById('help-open').addEventListener('click',()=>dialog.showModal());dialog.querySelector('[data-close-help]').addEventListener('click',()=>dialog.close());dialog.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target===dialog){const r=dialog.getBoundingClientRect();if(e.clientX<r.left||e.clientX>r.right||e.clientY<r.top||e.clientY>r.bottom)dialog.close();}});})();</script>
